On Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:19:06 +0000, claude <claude@p7x.dev> wrote:
> Changes in v4:
> - Fix the poudriere build, which failed in extract with "rm: go.mod:
>   Permission denied": post-fetch now writes go.mod in DIST_SUBDIR only
>   when its content changes, so the unprivileged re-run of fetch in
>   extract writes nothing.
> - Replace SONIC_BUMP with SONIC_EDIT, which carries the whole command.
> - Link to v3: id:356655d2db87becaa2f3c491e1de4b0df1664e6d.1792026153.git.claude@p7x.dev

This revision went out without an interdiff. Here it is, backfilled as
you asked in "New patch series must have an interdiff" [1]. Both
versions were rebuilt from the list with series-rebuild.sh, from "[PATCH
v2 0/4] Require an interdiff on revised series" [3], and the rebuilt v4
is identical to the commit it was formatted from. v3 and v4 share the
base 8e18e3939be9, so the interdiff below is the plain diff between the
two.

Interdiff against v3:
diff --git a/net-mgmt/signoz/Makefile b/net-mgmt/signoz/Makefile
index 82a81c589f2b..2b84b2ac713c 100644
--- a/net-mgmt/signoz/Makefile
+++ b/net-mgmt/signoz/Makefile
@@ -30,19 +30,21 @@ USERS=		${PORTNAME}
 GROUPS=		${PORTNAME}
 
 # sonic v1.14.1, as pinned upstream, builds only with Go 1.24 and 1.25
-SONIC_BUMP=	-require=github.com/bytedance/sonic@v1.15.4 \
+SONIC_EDIT=	${SETENVI} ${WRK_ENV} ${GO_ENV} ${GO_CMD} mod edit \
+		-require=github.com/bytedance/sonic@v1.15.4 \
 		-require=github.com/bytedance/sonic/loader@v0.5.2
 
-# before go-post-fetch, so it downloads the modules of the bumped go.mod
+# before go-post-fetch, so it downloads the modules of the bumped go.mod;
+# extract runs fetch again without write access, so write only on change
 post-fetch:
-	@(cd ${DISTDIR}/${DIST_SUBDIR} && ${RM} go.mod && \
-		${CP} ${GO_MODFILE} go.mod && \
-		${SETENVI} ${WRK_ENV} ${GO_ENV} ${GO_CMD} mod edit ${SONIC_BUMP})
+	@cd ${DISTDIR}/${DIST_SUBDIR} || exit 1; \
+	${SONIC_EDIT} -print ${GO_MODFILE} | \
+		${DIFF} -q - go.mod >/dev/null 2>&1 || \
+		{ ${RM} go.mod && ${SONIC_EDIT} -print ${GO_MODFILE} > go.mod; }
 
 # before go-post-extract, so it vendors the bumped modules
 post-extract:
-	@(cd ${WRKSRC} && \
-		${SETENVI} ${WRK_ENV} ${GO_ENV} ${GO_CMD} mod edit ${SONIC_BUMP})
+	@cd ${WRKSRC} && ${SONIC_EDIT}
 
 post-patch:
 	${REINPLACE_CMD} -e 's|/etc/signoz/web|${DATADIR}/web|' \

